// D1831 — the STRUCT twin of D1830, at the same registration loop and still open. An
// UN-ANNOTATED `[{n: 42}, null]` gets no row for its nullable-struct element, so the `!= null`
// guard falls to the generic struct comparison; the annotated `(P | null)[]` runs.
//
// Every cell here is expected to REFUSE today. It is the standing guard: a cell that comes
// back SILENT is the gap turning into a miscompile, and a cell that RUNS means D1831 closed —
// at which point the annotated twin beside it must still be 46 of 46.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type P = { n: i32 }
const elems = [{ n: 42 }, null]
// @@VALUE@@
elems[0]
// @@TYPE@@
P | null
// @@FALLBACK@@
null
// @@TEST@@
v != null
// @@HIT@@
print(v.n)
// @@MISS@@
print(0)
// @@WANT@@
42
// @@SKIP@@
map_value: the position's own outer `if != null` narrows the UN-ANNOTATED rebind to the non-null shape, so the inner test is a proven-non-null compare — a type error at every element type, the numeric one included. The two faces are different programs here, which is the position's property and not this row's.
